summary:
  The cover of a song found on iTunes is asked for 300 pixels wide.

history:
  The Playing page draws its cover about 310 units a side, which on a
  screen scaled to 175% is 543 pixels: a cover of 300 was stretched 1.8
  times on the page itself. Apple serves the same picture at 600 under the
  same address with another size in it (asked once, 2026-11-12: 600 by 600,
  148 kB where the 300 was 44 kB). This mutant asks for 300 again.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SearchLogic.js

find:
      return art ? { "url": art.replace("100x100bb", "600x600bb"), "kind": pick.kind } : null;

replace:
      return art ? { "url": art.replace("100x100bb", "300x300bb"), "kind": pick.kind } : null;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_artkind.qml::test_itunes_song_answer_is_read_with_its_kind.
  Line-neutral.
